jsntrs is a JSONata 2.x query and transformation engine written in Rust.

JSONata was originally created by Andrew Coleman and is maintained by the
jsonata-js project: https://github.com/jsonata-js/jsonata

jsntrs began as a Rust port of gnata, an independent Go implementation of
JSONata (https://github.com/recolabs/gnata). gnata's behavior served as the
reference for this port; docs/spec.md documents that behavior and cites the
Go sources, which live in the gnata repository, not this one.

Materials in testdata/ are derived from the upstream jsonata-js test suite;
attribution and the upstream MIT license text are reproduced verbatim in
testdata/NOTICE.

